# Shell scripts and Python tools in this repo are executed inside a Linux
# Docker container (see docker/*/Dockerfile). Force LF line endings so a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true doesn't corrupt their shebang
# lines (this broke `RUN ./llvm.sh 14` in the Docker build in practice).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# setbench's TPC-C schema files are parsed with a plain C++ getline() loop
# that does not strip \r -- a CRLF line ending corrupts the parsed table/
# index names, which std::map::operator[] "resolves" by silently inserting
# a null-valued entry instead of failing, crashing the first thread that
# reads it (not necessarily at schema-parse time, so this can look like an
# unrelated, thread-count-dependent segfault deep into the workload run).
# This bit us once already from a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true;
# force LF so it can't recur.
artifact/patches/setbench-tpcc/macrobench/benchmarks/*.txt text eol=lf
